  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 213 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nThe upper level low will slowly move out of northern Mexico and\ninto southwest Texas on Sunday and Sunday night further increasing\nlarge scale forcing for ascent. Rain chances remain high (60-90%)\non Saturday night into Sunday afternoon from the Concho Valley \nsouthward into the Northern Edwards Plateau. The RRFS continues to\nshow more widespread rainfall totals of a half an inch to near 2 \ninches south of I-20, while the ensembles and GFS continue to focus\nthe heaviest rainfall amounts closer to the I-10 corridor. As\nsuch. will continue with the highest PoPs roughly from San Angelo\nsouthward. Day 2 marginal risk for excessive rainfall remains in\nplace for the southern half of the area but not looking at much in\nthe way of widespread flash flooding overall. Will leave some \nrain chances in the forecast for Monday (mainly in the morning \nhours) with the rest of the work week looking dry. Temperatures on\nSunday will be in the 60s before warming back up into the mid to \nupper 70s through the middle of next week.",
